## Task 6 proven repair — Membership audit authority

Fresh audit found that `app/Memberships/routes.php` selected the audit event from HTTP input `$decision` while the frozen F22 contract requires the canonical returned `charge_outcome`.

- RED commit: `4aec788ec4805b5008e5fc7dd96bed0f37f430c8`.
- CI #995 PHP 8.3: 599 tests / 6410 assertions / exactly 1 failure.
- Failure: expected `membership.charge_skipped`; actual `membership.charge_created` when request input and service outcome intentionally diverged.
- GREEN commit: `edbac36b5033446ae710f97e3b81659abc24c0cc`.
- Minimal repair: event authority now derives from `($result['charge_outcome'] ?? null) === 'created'`.
- PHP 8.3 on CI #996: 599 tests / 6412 assertions / 0 failures / 0 errors.
- Merge still requires #996 all-success on PHP 8.3/8.4/8.5 before this Closure Head is published.

