## 10-pass closure audit

1. **Scope:** PASS — F22 only; no F23 product work.
2. **KISS budget:** PASS — one table, one domain class, no new permission/dependency/event bus/auth stack/scheduler.
3. **Authority uniqueness:** PASS — `AuditService` owns audit persistence; existing business services remain owners; `NotificationService` owns notification retention.
4. **Anti-fanout:** PASS — audit is explicit at approved route owners; no cross-domain event infrastructure.
5. **Secrets/privacy:** PASS — audit metadata is bounded and rejects secret-shaped keys; password/reset token/temp credential/document/payment bodies are not recorded.
6. **Tenant IDOR:** PASS — ownership-first lease resolution remains before child lookups across tenant surfaces.
7. **Auth/CSRF/session:** PASS — global boundaries preserved; exact protected cron exception remains bounded; production cookie policy is tested.
8. **Storage/headers/external URLs:** PASS — private storage stays fail-closed; common headers remain centralized; audit viewer is `private, no-store`; WhatsApp provider URL remains HTTPS-only and isolated from candidate continuation capability.
9. **Retention/evidence:** PASS — terminal recipient name/email redaction is strict `< 90 days`, idempotent and preserves operational evidence.
10. **Governance:** PRODUCT PASS / REPOSITORY ACTION REQUIRED — `main` reports unprotected and no required checks in current remote evidence.

